// Gen9 scene (op 6): fill (0), tone over (1), image copy (4) and premultiplied image over (11), the images with an optional R/B
// swap (0x80), drawn in order over the damage. A thread is a strip of eight 8 by 8 pixel tiles, 64 pixels by 8 rows: walker group X
// (r0.1) is the strip's column of 64 pixels and Y (r0.6) its row of tiles, its first pixel at x = px0 + 64 X, y = py0 + 8 Y. Every
// ALU instruction is SIMD8 (a register, one row of a tile), so the Gen7 and Gen7.5 patch of these words (gpu.c's gpu_start) has
// no compressed instruction to change.
//
// CURBE (r1): r1.1 = px0, r1.2 = py0, r1.3 = px1, r1.4 = py1 (the damage, in the picture's pixels).
// Binding table entry 0 is the damage (a tile read once, at the first record that draws in it, only when no record covers it
// whole and opaque, and written once if anything drew); entry 1 the cells' lists: the damage in cells of 64 by 64 pixels from
// px0, py0, a cell eight rows of 64 bytes at x = 64 X, y = 8 * (Y / 8) (a row a record, 32 bytes used: kind, x0, y0, x1, y1, then
// colour or the image's x and row bias and its entry), the first row's word 0 with the list's length in its bits 31:16, 0x100 for
// a list of more than eight (the row is then no record: its word 1 is the list's first row in entry 2, whose rows are records)
// and 0x200 when the first record covers every tile of the cell whole and opaque (no tile is read, none looks for its cover);
// entries 3 and up are the records' images, a surface each (its own base and pitch), read a tile at a time at byte
// x = word 5 + 4 x and row = word 6 + y. The records are clipped to the damage, and a cell's list starts at the last record that
// covers all of the cell's damage, by the encoder (gpu_i915_scene_batch). A strip reads its cell's list once.
//
// A tile: the last record that covers it whole and opaque is found (a fill, or a copy: what was under it cannot show), and the
// records from it on are drawn (or from the first, over the tile as it was read). A tile row is written under its lanes' mask,
// x in [x0, x1) and the row's y in [y0, y1).
//
// Registers: r2 scalars (.0 bx .1 by .2 bx + 8 .3 the tile's bottom .4 the record .5 the first drawn .6 the batch of eight
// records held in r40-r47 .7 4 bx), r4 (.0 the strip's end .1 the list's first row in entry 2 .2 the list's length .3 its flags
// .4 the tile is in r14-r21), r3 the lanes' x, r7 the lane numbers 0 to 7, r8 scratch, r9 the x mask, r10 the rows' y masks
// (lane r: row r), r11 r12 r13 the headers of the lists', the image's and the tile's block messages, r14-r21 the tile, r22-r29
// the image's tile, r30-r38 scratch, r39 the record drawn (moved from the batch by its number: r[a0.0]), r40-r47 the batch.
mov (1|M0)               r7.0<1>:ud    0:ud
mov (1|M0)               r7.1<1>:ud    1:ud
mov (1|M0)               r7.2<1>:ud    2:ud
mov (1|M0)               r7.3<1>:ud    3:ud
mov (1|M0)               r7.4<1>:ud    4:ud
mov (1|M0)               r7.5<1>:ud    5:ud
